# Every dependence somebody observed between two layers' remainders. One row per
# (filing, from_layer, to_layer).
#
# Every row contradicts the assumption
#   This model assumes layers hold their remainders independently, so every row here is somebody
#   contradicting that with an observation. That is why the observation is required: a coupling is
#   never worked out, never inferred from correlation, and never filed as a number alone. Somebody
#   watched two layers move together and wrote down what they saw.
#
# No rows says nothing by itself
#   A filing with no couplings has either a stack of independent layers or nobody who looked, and
#   those are opposite claims. Which one it is lives in `coupling_search` (see
#   epistemics/searches.sqlc), not in this relation. Filled out into a grid of 0.0, the difference
#   is gone for good.
-- pm:Stack/pm:couplings/pm:coupling, each carrying its pm:observed.
SELECT c.filing, c.from_layer, c.to_layer,
       c.low, c.mode, c.high, c.unit, c.strength_absent, c.observation
FROM pm.coupling c
